# {{pretty_name}}

<!-- What this dataset is, who made it and why, in two or three sentences. -->
An example of a dataset derived from [GoldenCheetah OpenData](https://huggingface.co/datasets/GoldenCheetah/opendata):
the {{n_activities}} activities of {{n_athletes}} athletes that have a time series, resampled to
one row per second.

It follows the [GoldenCheetah dataset conventions](https://github.com/GoldenCheetah/OpenData/blob/master/huggingface/CONVENTIONS.md):
`athlete_id` and `activity_id` are those of OpenData, so the tables join directly to it, and
shared columns (`power_w`, `hr_bpm`, ...) have the same name, type, unit and meaning there.

## Usage

```python
import polars as pl

acts = pl.read_parquet("hf://datasets/{{repo_id}}/data/activities/*.parquet")
ts = pl.scan_parquet("hf://datasets/{{repo_id}}/data/timeseries/*.parquet")
```

